WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.463
Why GitHub Actions?

2
00:00:01.463 --> 00:00:04.536
Learn documents two ways
to run a scheduled job

3
00:00:04.536 --> 00:00:07.374
that signs in to Azure
with no stored secret.

4
00:00:07.374 --> 00:00:10.300
The chapter picks GitHub
Actions for two reasons.

5
00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:13.417
Learn publishes complete
sample workflows for it,

6
00:00:13.417 --> 00:00:16.238
on one page, and that's
where the chapter starts.

7
00:00:16.238 --> 00:00:21.563
And the sign-in action is Microsoft's own,
with its source and its inputs published.

8
00:00:21.563 --> 00:00:26.701
An agency standardized on Azure Pipelines
can still use the same comparator,

9
00:00:26.701 --> 00:00:30.140
packager and tests; only
the workflow file changes.
